# Report retention policy (V6).
#
# V5 published every number in docs/V5_RESEARCH_REPORT.md from files that were
# ignored here, so the results existed only as untracked local artifacts. That
# breaks the project's own reproducibility rule: a result must not depend on an
# undocumented local file. V6 changes the rule rather than the results.
#
# COMMITTED: timestamped reports. They are immutable evidence - one file per
# run, never overwritten, carrying dataset and split fingerprints, seeds,
# threshold, environment and the exact command.
#
# IGNORED: the `latest-*` pointers and the V2 detection-eval output below. A
# pointer is mutable by construction, so committing it would mean rewriting a
# tracked file on every run - the opposite of an immutable artifact. Regenerate
# a pointer by re-running; read history from the timestamped files.

latest.json
latest-v4-experiments-*.json
latest-v5-*.json
latest-v6-*.json
latest-v7-*.json
latest-v8-*.json

# V2 detection evaluation: regenerated by the /detection/quality endpoint on
# demand and not a published research artifact.
detection-eval-*.json
